{"title":"Career Roadmap: Urban Researcher","role":"Urban Researcher","summary":"An Urban Researcher studies how cities, towns, and regions function, grow, and change. The role combines urban planning, spatial analysis, statistics, economics, mobility, housing, environmental science, policy research, and data analytics to generate evidence for better urban decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Plan"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["ID","Level","Discipline","Degree","Specialization","Target Career"],"rows":[[{"text":"635"},{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Architecture, Planning & Design"},{"text":"B.Plan (Bachelor of Planning)"},{"text":"Housing / Transport / Environmental Planning"},{"text":"Urban Researcher"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Urban Researcher studies how cities, towns, and regions function, grow, and change. The role combines urban planning, spatial analysis, statistics, economics, mobility, housing, environmental science, policy research, and data analytics to generate evidence for better urban decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"Urban Researchers may investigate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Housing affordability"},{"text":"Urban growth"},{"text":"Transportation and mobility"},{"text":"Land-use change"},{"text":"Informal settlements"},{"text":"Climate resilience"},{"text":"Urban poverty and inequality"},{"text":"Public infrastructure"},{"text":"Environmental conditions"},{"text":"Urban governance"},{"text":"Migration and demographics"},{"text":"Public-space usage"},{"text":"Regional development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest modern profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Urban Planning","Research Methodology","GIS","Statistics","Data Science","Policy Analysis"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–